{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he said in his heart.</b> Of the wicked it is said <b>in his heart</b>: 'ויאמר עשו בלבו' (Gen. 27:41), 'ויאמר המן בלבו' (Esth. 5:12), and of the righteous it is said <b>upon his heart</b>: 'וישם דניאל על לבו' (Dan. 1:8), 'וישת דוד את הדבר על לבו' (1 Sam. 21:13) — to teach you that the heart of the righteous is in their hand, but the wicked are in the hand of their heart. And what is written here <b>in his heart</b> is because in this matter he was expressing wonder in his heart: 'Shall a man of a hundred years have a child?' — and it appears as though he did not believe the tidings."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:31.116147728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}